                                                "sense_id": "a50da932-2932-3b90-92f8-a78a535b2a2e",
                                                "text": "Put differently, the active ingredients in crime seem to be structural disadvantage and attenuated collective efficacy more so than disorder. Attacking public disorder through tough policing may thus be a politically popular but perhaps analytically weak strategy to reduce crime, mainly because such a strategy leaves the common origins of both […] untouched."
                                            }
